g></a></div></div></div><svg class="main-svg" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" width="694" height="494"><g class="hoverlayer"></g></svg></div></div></div></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(470,20)" x="470" y="20" title="codeHTML" width="560" height="419" class="codeHTML" name="codeHTML" rot="0"><foreignObject x="0" y="0" width="560" height="419" style="width: 560px; height: 419px;"><div name="htmlCode" style="zoom: 0.56; height: 748.214px; width: 1000px;" code="&lt;div class=&quot;ch&quot;&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Counter, D flip-flop and RC filter: bits and a bus in the wave viewer&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;ch-card&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Circuit Components&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clock (CK):&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;DigitalClock&lt;/em&gt;, 1 MHz, duty 0.5, first rising edge at 0.5 &amp;micro;s&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Counter (CN):&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;Counter&lt;/em&gt;, 3 bits: counts the rising edges of &lt;em&gt;clk&lt;/em&gt;; its outputs are the bus &lt;em&gt;s[0:2]&lt;/em&gt; (bit 0 = LSB)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flip-flop (F0):&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;DFF&lt;/em&gt; with D wired to its own inverted output &lt;em&gt;nq0&lt;/em&gt;: it toggles at every edge, so &lt;em&gt;q0&lt;/em&gt; is &lt;em&gt;clk&lt;/em&gt; divided by 2&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Filter (RC, CP):&lt;/strong&gt; 2 k&amp;Omega; and 0.5 nF on &lt;em&gt;q0&lt;/em&gt;, output &lt;em&gt;lp&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Netlist&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ch-formula&quot;&gt;
CK = DigitalClock(&quot;clk&quot;)&lt;br&gt;
CN = Counter(&quot;clk&quot;, [&quot;s0&quot;, &quot;s1&quot;, &quot;s2&quot;])&lt;br&gt;
F0 = DFF(&quot;nq0&quot;, &quot;clk&quot;, &quot;q0&quot;, &quot;nq0&quot;)&lt;br&gt;
RC = Resistor(&quot;q0&quot;, &quot;lp&quot;) &amp;nbsp; CP = Capacitor(&quot;lp&quot;, &quot;0&quot;)
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Digital outputs&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In the properties of the analysis, the rows &lt;em&gt;clk&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;q0&lt;/em&gt; (one bit each) and &lt;em&gt;count&lt;/em&gt; (the three bits &lt;em&gt;s0 s1 s2&lt;/em&gt;) are digital outputs, added with &lt;em&gt;Add output&lt;/em&gt; in &lt;em&gt;Y axe outputs&lt;/em&gt;. A bit is drawn as a step trace; a bus is drawn as a hexagon holding its value, in hex, bin or dec (&lt;em&gt;Format&lt;/em&gt;). The threshold between 0 and 1 is 2.5 V (&lt;em&gt;Logic threshold&lt;/em&gt;). &lt;em&gt;lp&lt;/em&gt; stays an analog output, drawn below. The value inside a narrow hexagon appears after a zoom.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;ch-grid&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ch-col blue&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Results (0 &amp;hellip; 20 &amp;micro;s)&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;count&lt;/em&gt; goes 0, 1, &amp;hellip; 7, 0 &amp;hellip; and changes at each rising edge (0.52 &amp;micro;s, 1.52 &amp;micro;s, &amp;hellip;)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;q0&lt;/em&gt; toggles at each edge: period 2 &amp;micro;s&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;lp&lt;/em&gt; settles between 1.41 V and 3.59 V (RC = 1 &amp;micro;s, a triangle-like wave around 2.5 V)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ch-col green&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Things to try&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Change &lt;em&gt;Format&lt;/em&gt; of &lt;em&gt;count&lt;/em&gt; to &lt;em&gt;bin&lt;/em&gt; or &lt;em&gt;dec&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the threshold to a band such as &lt;em&gt;1,4&lt;/em&gt;: a value inside it is drawn red (unknown)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Raise the counter size by renaming the bus (for example &lt;em&gt;s[0:3]&lt;/em&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
"> 
    <!-- Parent container that responds to mouse movement -->
    <div class="chtool"> 
        
        <!-- tool bar-->
        <div class="ch-page-toolbar" style="zoom: 1.78571;">
            <button class="ch-toolbar-button" title="Home">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
                    <path d="M12 3 L3 10 V21 H9 V15 H15 V21 H21 V10 Z"></path>
                </svg>
            </button>
            <button class="ch-toolbar-button" title="Modified" onclick="modifyAction()">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
                    <path d="M3 17.25V21h3.75L17.81 9.94l-3.75-3.75L3 17.25zM20.71 7.04c.39-.39.39-1.02 0-1.41l-2.34-2.34c-.39-.39-1.02-.39-1.41 0l-1.83 1.83 3.75 3.75 1.83-1.83z"></path>
                </svg>
            </button>
        </div>

       <div class="ch">
<h1>Counter, D flip-flop and RC filter: bits and a bus in the wave viewer</h1>

<div class="ch-card">
<h2>Circuit Components</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Clock (CK):</strong> <em>DigitalClock</em>, 1 MHz, duty 0.5, first rising edge at 0.5 µs</li>
<li><strong>Counter (CN):</strong> <em>Counter</em>, 3 bits: counts the rising edges of <em>clk</em>; its outputs are the bus <em>s[0:2]</em> (bit 0 = LSB)</li>
<li><strong>Flip-flop (F0):</strong> <em>DFF</em> with D wired to its own inverted output <em>nq0</em>: it toggles at every edge, so <em>q0</em> is <em>clk</em> divided by 2</li>
<li><strong>Filter (RC, CP):</strong> 2 kΩ and 0.5 nF on <em>q0</em>, output <em>lp</em></li>
</ul>
</div>

<h2>Netlist</h2>
<div class="ch-formula">
CK = DigitalClock("clk")<br>
CN = Counter("clk", ["s0", "s1", "s2"])<br>
F0 = DFF("nq0", "clk", "q0", "nq0")<br>
RC = Resistor("q0", "lp") &nbsp; CP = Capacitor("lp", "0")
</div>

<h2>Digital outputs</h2>
<p>In the properties of the analysis, the rows <em>clk</em>, <em>q0</em> (one bit each) and <em>count</em> (the three bits <em>s0 s1 s2</em>) are digital outputs, added with <em>Add output</em> in <em>Y axe outputs</em>. A bit is drawn as a step trace; a bus is drawn as a hexagon holding its value, in hex, bin or dec (<em>Format</em>). The threshold between 0 and 1 is 2.5 V (<em>Logic threshold</em>). <em>lp</em> stays an analog output, drawn below. The value inside a narrow hexagon appears after a zoom.</p>

<div class="ch-grid">
<div class="ch-col blue">
<h3>Results (0 … 20 µs)</h3>
<ul>
<li><em>count</em> goes 0, 1, … 7, 0 … and changes at each rising edge (0.52 µs, 1.52 µs, …)</li>
<li><em>q0</em> toggles at each edge: period 2 µs</li>
<li><em>lp</em> settles between 1.41 V and 3.59 V (RC = 1 µs, a triangle-like wave around 2.5 V)</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div class="ch-col green">
<h3>Things to try</h3>
<ul>
<li>Change <em>Format</em> of <em>count</em> to <em>bin</em> or <em>dec</em></li>
<li>Set the threshold to a band such as <em>1,4</em>: a value inside it is drawn red (unknown)</li>
<li>Raise the counter size by renaming the bus (for example <em>s[0:3]</em>)</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</div>

    </div>
    </div></foreignObject></g>